    <statement><p>What angle (in degrees) corresponds to 17.7 rotations around the unit circle?</p>
<p>17.7 rotations is an angle of <fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/> degrees.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6372</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



If we go around 17.7 times, we make 17.7 full circles, which is
<m>17.7\cdot 360^{\circ} = 6372^{\circ}</m> .



</solution>
